dkg — provenance note
=====================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `frost`/
`threshold_ecdsa`/`bls12_381` self-contained crypto modules, not folded into
the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

dkg — Phase 1 (secret-key distributed key generation) scaffold for a secure,
dealer-free key generation feeding this repo's `threshold_ecdsa`. Clean-room
from one public paper:

  - R. Gennaro, S. Jarecki, H. Krawczyk, T. Rabin, "Secure Distributed Key
    Generation for Discrete-Log Based Cryptosystems", Journal of Cryptology
    20(1), 2007 (earlier EUROCRYPT '99) — "GJKR". The construction this module
    targets: Pedersen-VSS Round 1, complaint/QUAL Round 2, and the
    Pedersen-then-Feldman-after-QUAL bias-prevented public-key extraction.

A public specification/paper, not a copyrightable work (merger doctrine — see
`CONVENTIONS.md` §5); the entry is included for provenance clarity given the
module's crypto-protocol nature. No third-party SOURCE was ported or consulted.

The mechanical layer reuses this repo's OWN prior work: the Shamir/Feldman
share arithmetic and `KeyShare`/`Element`/`Scalar` surface come from
`threshold_ecdsa` (itself a field/group-swapped port of this repo's `frost`/
`bls12_381.threshold` — same authorship). `paillier` is a build dependency,
attached to DKG outputs by `assembleKeyShares` (thin, judgment-free
composition). `std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1` (curve group, `basePoint`, `add`/
`mul`, `fromSec1`), `std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1.scalar.Scalar` (Zq arithmetic),
and `std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256` (for the nothing-up-my-sleeve Pedersen
generator `h`) are used via their public APIs only — the same primitives
`frost`/`threshold_ecdsa` already build on. No new curve, field, or hash
primitive is implemented here.

The FINAL end-to-end verification target,
`std.crypto.sign.ecdsa.EcdsaSecp256k1Sha256`, is Zig's own standard-library
ECDSA, used via its public API.

Status: COMPLETE (Phase 1). The five irreducible GJKR protocol-soundness
functions in `core.zig` (`verifyPedersenShare`, `verifyFeldmanShare`,
`computeQual`, `deriveGroupPublicKey`, `combineKeyShare`) are implemented and
`gate.fable_core_implemented` is `true` — see each function's doc comment and
`SPEC.md` for the exact construction. No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or
copied anywhere in this module.
